# Project memory

- The root README must say what the product does, how to run it, and what remains unfinished.
- Non-trivial feature contracts live in `docs/specs/` with observable acceptance criteria.
- Record durable decisions with context and consequence; do not turn the README into a live task tracker.
- Update docs when behavior, setup, configuration, or user-visible workflow changes.
- Verify referenced paths and commands before publishing documentation.
